P=pathlib.Path('/workspace/improvement');D=P/'execution_tradeoff'
def read(p):return json.loads(p.read_text())
def main():
 r=read(D/'results.json');s=read(D/'pilot/source-summary.json')['summary'];g=read(D/'pilot/generation-result.json');old=read(D/'saved_diagnosis.json');a=r['loops']['twice'];b=r['loops']['once'];cost=r['costs'];forecast=r['forecasts'];now=datetime.datetime.now(zoneinfo.ZoneInfo('Asia/Taipei')).strftime('%d %B %Y, %H:%M Asia/Taipei')
 table='| Condition | N | WER % | DNSMOS | NISQA | UTMOS | Joint gate |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n'
 names={'raw50':'FV50, reused decoder graph','stft_identity':'STFT round-trip control','anchor25':'25% reconstruction-spectrum anchor'}
 for k in ['raw50','stft_identity','anchor25']:
  v=s[k];q=v['quality'];table+=f"| {names[k]} | {v['count']} | {v['error_percent']:.4f} | {q['dnsmos']:.4f} | {q['nisqa']:.4f} | {q['utmos']:.4f} | {'pass' if r['joint_gates'][k]['joint_pass'] else 'fail'} |\n"
 decision='A source/quality candidate exists but requires frozen selection and a feasible next-stage budget before advancement.' if r['candidate'] else 'The pilot completed normally, but no condition passed the unchanged joint gate. Selection is scientific stop; candidate is null. Validation and transfer/defense tests remain gated off.'
 speed=100*r['paired_speed_reduction_fraction'];ci=r['paired_speed_reduction_bootstrap95_ci'];mem_a=a['peak_allocated_bytes']/1024**3;mem_b=b['peak_allocated_bytes']/1024**3;du=r['quality_delta_anchor_vs_raw'];pp=g['preprocessing'];exact=sum(v['exact_cached_features'] for v in pp['records'])
 lines=[f'# Joint quality and efficiency pilot results\n\nUpdated {now}. [Protocol](20_quality_efficiency_protocol.md) · [source audit](19_source_audit.md) · [complete measurements](execution_tradeoff/results.json) · [per-recording latency](execution_tradeoff/latency_per_recording.csv).\n',f'{decision}\n',
 '## What was tested and why\n\nThe cheapest completed strong original setting already exceeded 75% WER, but failed UTMOS. Longer runs were much slower and did not repair quality. We tested two separable ideas: reuse the decoder graph to remove duplicate rendering while retaining the exact attack; then apply one fixed spectral repair to that 50-step attack. This is an engineering improvement and mechanism experiment, not a new generator or a novelty claim.\n',
 f'The earlier strong FV50 loop averaged {old["methods"]["single_50"]["mean_seconds_per_recording"]:.2f} seconds/recording; FV1500 averaged {old["methods"]["single_1500"]["mean_seconds_per_recording"]:.2f}. Historical S/D/I and spectrum diagnostics are in [saved_diagnosis.json](execution_tradeoff/saved_diagnosis.json). Insertions were important but not dominant. Higher distortion correlated only weakly with UTMOS, so spectral damage was a testable explanation, not an established cause. Absolute smoothness/high-frequency penalties do not directly preserve phonetic content.\n',
 '## Recognition and quality on all 48 recordings\n\nThe cohort is unchanged: 48 exposed development recordings, 30 speakers, 360.010 seconds, 994 reference words. The fixed gate remains WER >75%, DNSMOS OVRL >=3, NISQA MOS >=3.75 and UTMOS >=3.5.\n',table,
 f'The repair changed pooled WER by **{du["wer_percentage_points"]:+.4f} percentage points** and mean UTMOS by **{du["quality"]["utmos"]:+.4f}**. DNSMOS changed {du["quality"]["dnsmos"]:+.4f}; NISQA changed {du["quality"]["nisqa"]:+.4f}. The predeclared quality mechanism signal (+.15 UTMOS with no more than 5 WER-point loss) was {"met" if r["quality_mechanism_signal"] else "not met"}. This secondary signal never replaces the joint gate.\n',
 'The anchor moves log magnitudes 25% toward the same HiFi-GAN neutral reconstruction, retaining attacked STFT phase, with one inverse transform and no phase iterations, normalization or clipping. The STFT round-trip control isolates transform/reconstruction effects. Achieved spectrum differences and spectrogram inconsistency are recorded in [achieved_spectra.json](execution_tradeoff/achieved_spectra.json); a target complex spectrum is not automatically realizable. A WER decrease is consistent with removing magnitude information used by Whisper, but does not uniquely establish mechanism. Automatic MOS and ASR do not establish what humans understand. No listening or blinded-human scores are invented.\n',
 '## Matched efficiency measurements\n\nEvery clip ran both paths in alternating order on the same TITAN RTX, float32, batch one, identical cached features, source, objective, 50 Adam updates, projection and checkpointing. The same phase timing/synchronization and allocator-cache policy applied to both. Each pair and every generated raw waveform matched the frozen single50 output exactly. New fresh feature extraction was profiled separately; '+f'{exact}/48 fresh tensors were bit-identical to the canonical cached tensor, and all passed the frozen numerical tolerance. The canonical cache was used for the paired comparison.\n',
 '| Path | Mean sec/recording | p50 sec | p95 sec | Sec/audio sec | Loop wall min | CUDA-event min | Peak allocated GiB | Peak reserved GiB |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|',
 *[f'| {label} | {v["latency_seconds"]["mean"]:.3f} | {v["latency_seconds"]["p50"]:.3f} | {v["latency_seconds"]["p95"]:.3f} | {v["seconds_per_audio_second"]:.3f} | {v["wall_seconds"]/60:.3f} | {v["gpu_event_seconds"]/60:.3f} | {v["peak_allocated_bytes"]/1024**3:.3f} | {v["peak_reserved_bytes"]/1024**3:.3f} |' for label,v in [('Original twice-render loop',a),('Retained decoder graph',b)]],
 f'\nAggregate loop wall time fell **{speed:.2f}%**; paired-recording bootstrap 95% interval {100*ci[0]:.2f}–{100*ci[1]:.2f}%. This interval describes variation over these 48 recordings in one system session, not repeat-system uncertainty. The proposed >=10% reduction/<20 GiB allocated-memory engineering target was {"met" if r["efficiency_target_pass"] else "not met"}. Peak memory changed {mem_a:.3f} → {mem_b:.3f} GiB. Report that memory tradeoff alongside speed. This removes exactly one decoder forward per step, not recognizer backpropagation or Whisper activation recomputation. Raw quality and attack strength remain identical.\n',
 '| Phase, all 48 | Original seconds | Retained-graph seconds |\n|---|---:|---:|',
 *[f'| {phase.replace("_"," ")} | {a["phase_wall_seconds"][phase]:.3f} | {b["phase_wall_seconds"][phase]:.3f} |' for phase in a['phase_wall_seconds']],
 f'\nSource forward/backward pairs remained {a["source_forward_backward_pairs"]:,} per path. Decoder forwards fell {a["decoder_forwards"]:,} → {b["decoder_forwards"]:,}; backwards stayed {b["decoder_backwards"]:,}. Internal checkpoint recomputation is additional work. Full per-recording wall, seconds/audio-second, GPU-stream elapsed time and memory are in the linked CSV; per-phase traces are in `execution_tradeoff/pilot/timings/`.\n',
 '## Complete costs and conditional scale forecast\n',
 '| Cost category | Measured seconds | Interpretation |\n|---|---:|---|',
 f'| Feature preprocessing, 48 clips | {cost["feature_preprocessing"]:.3f} | Fresh WavLM extraction, profiled separately |',
 f'| Teacher/generation, reused graph | {cost["teacher_generation"]:.3f} | Necessary 50-step per-new-recording search |',
 f'| Spectrum repair, 48 clips | {cost["spectral_repair"]:.3f} | Additional CPU computation; search cost is still charged |',
 f'| Shared paired-record IO/setup/comparison/output overhead | {cost["shared_record_io_setup_comparison_overhead_seconds"]:.3f} | Conservatively charged in full to candidate forecasts; includes extra comparison work |',
 f'| Model loading | {cost["model_loading"]:.3f} | Encoder plus source/decoder cold loads |',
 f'| Generation warmup | {cost["warmup"]:.3f} | Excluded from matched loop speed estimate |',
 '| New learned training | 0 | No student trained |',
 f'| Formal evaluation, 144 scored outputs | {cost["formal_evaluation"]["elapsed_wall_seconds"]:.3f} | Includes source/scorer loading and overhead |',
 f'| Recognition within evaluation | {cost["formal_evaluation"]["asr_wall_seconds"]:.3f} | Measured separately |',
 f'| Quality within evaluation | {cost["formal_evaluation"]["quality_wall_seconds"]:.3f} | Measured separately |',
 f'| GPU-job process wall (allocation upper bound) | {cost["gpu_job_process_wall_upper_bound_seconds"]:.3f} | Generation + evaluation process durations; includes CPU/setup/idle; not kernel-active time |',
 f'| Entire paired experiment | {cost["measured_full_cycle_wall_seconds"]:.3f} | Runs both generation paths; under 2,700-second ceiling |',
 f'\nThe generation process wall duration was {cost["measured_generation_process_gpu_allocation_wall_seconds"]/3600:.4f} hours. Together with evaluation the GPU-job process wall upper bound is {cost["gpu_job_process_wall_upper_bound_seconds"]/3600:.4f} hours, including setup/idle/I/O. Summed recorded CUDA-event intervals were {cost["measured_experiment_gpu_event_elapsed_seconds"]/3600:.4f} hours across the experiment, excluding some loading/warmup transfers. CUDA-event intervals may include host dispatch gaps and CPU work between events; neither this sum nor allocated wall hours is an exact kernel-active-hours or energy measurement. [Thirty-second sampled GPU utilization/memory](execution_tradeoff/gpu_samples.json) and peak allocated/reserved memory are retained; historical per-method peaks were unavailable.\n',
 f'Including fresh feature extraction, repair and all measured shared paired-record I/O/setup/comparison overhead conservatively charged to one path, the forecast for the selected implementation is {cost["candidate_steady_generation_seconds_excluding_loading"]/48:.3f} seconds/recording and {cost["candidate_steady_generation_seconds_excluding_loading"]/r["audio_seconds"]:.3f} seconds/audio-second, before amortized loading/warmup. This is an accounting forecast, not a separate direct single-path deployment latency measurement. Under the same duration/text distribution, hardware, precision and batch size, **1,000 new clips are forecast at {forecast["new1000_similar_recordings_hours"]:.3f} hours**, and **ten audio hours of teacher data at {forecast["teacher10_audio_hours_allocation_hours"]:.3f} allocated GPU-hours**. A new 48-point generation job is forecast at {forecast["new48_seconds_plus_measured_load_warmup"]/60:.3f} minutes including measured loading/warmup, before evaluation. These are conditional forecasts, not completed larger runs or a user-mandated latency limit.\n',
 'Whisper still uses its fixed 30-second input context; decoder and transcript costs vary with length. Longer training clips or changed batching need their own throughput check. Teacher-corpus scoring, training a reusable student, and actual student inference/retention are additional, unmeasured costs. A future break-even calculation must divide total teacher-data plus training cost by measured per-input time saved, after both teacher and student satisfy the unchanged gates. Cheap repair does not create a fast reusable attack.\n',
 '## Decision and evidence limits\n\n'+decision+' The raw implementation speed improvement is separately useful, but does not solve the quality failure or prove deployment scalability. Do not repeat this fixed repair fraction as a hidden sweep. The next experiment should address the measured quality/attack coupling or a better bounded recognition objective, with a matched cost forecast before launch. The data prepared for larger training remain unused in this cycle.\n\nNo 76-point validation, unseen-model transfer, original-defense persistence, untouched confirmation/final evaluation or human study ran. Existing frozen plans/code and exposed/untouched cohort boundaries are preserved. [Explicit exit receipt](execution_tradeoff/exit_receipt.json); [selection](execution_tradeoff/selection.json); [audio comparison](http://localhost:8888/).\n']
 if (D/'prepared_data_forecast.json').exists():
  prepared=read(D/'prepared_data_forecast.json');lines+=['## Prepared-data forecast with clip overhead\n\nThe prepared training recordings average about 12.8 seconds, versus 7.5 in the pilot. A fixed-context recognizer makes a duration-only forecast incomplete. Fit measured per-clip generation (including preprocessing/repair) as intercept + audio duration; this is a conditional workload model, not actual corpus throughput.\n',f'Fitted intercept {prepared["equation_seconds"]["intercept_per_clip"]:.3f} s/clip plus {prepared["equation_seconds"]["seconds_per_audio_second_slope"]:.3f} s/audio-second. Leave-one-recording-out mean absolute prediction error {prepared["diagnostics"]["leave_one_recording_out_mae_seconds"]:.3f} s ({prepared["diagnostics"]["leave_one_recording_out_mape_percent"]:.1f}% MAPE).\n','| Prepared corpus | Clips | Audio hours | Length-aware teacher generation hours | Count-only sensitivity hours | Duration-only sensitivity hours |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
  for name,v in prepared['datasets'].items():lines.append(f'| {name} | {v["count"]} | {v["audio_seconds"]/3600:.3f} | {v["predicted_teacher_generation_hours_excluding_loading_evaluation_training"]:.3f} | {v["count_only_sensitivity_hours"]:.3f} | {v["audio_duration_only_sensitivity_hours"]:.3f} |')
  lines+=['\nThese scenarios exclude one-time loading, corpus evaluation and all later student training; count/duration sensitivities are not uncertainty bounds. Model-parameter bootstrap intervals, duration-range coverage and limits are in [prepared_data_forecast.json](execution_tradeoff/prepared_data_forecast.json). Text/duration distribution and system shifts remain unmeasured: run a representative workload check before a long launch. No prepared training job was launched.\n']
 lines+=['## Publication objective\n\nThe user now explicitly asks for a contribution suitable for peer-reviewed speech/NLP research in the ACL theme. Decoder graph reuse and fixed spectrum blending are engineering/diagnostic steps, not sufficient evidence of method novelty. The next method must be positioned against the nearest primary prior work, test a falsifiable mechanism, and show quality/attack/compute gains under matched conditions; transfer, defense persistence and human intelligibility remain required evidence. See [publication positioning and contribution plan](22_publication_positioning.md). Acceptance cannot be inferred from a development pilot.\n']
 (P/'21_quality_efficiency_results.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
 for name in ['17_summary_and_next_steps.md','HANDOFF.md','audio_browser/README_AUDIO_BROWSER.md']:
  dest=D/('before_'+name.replace('/','_'));src=P/name
  if not dest.exists():shutil.copyfile(src,dest)
 p=P/'17_summary_and_next_steps.md';text=p.read_text();text=text.replace('[All 67 conditions as CSV]','[All conditions as CSV]').replace('**67 saved conditions and 2,664 scored recordings**','**70 saved conditions and 2,808 scored recordings**');intro=f'\n## Latest continuation: quality and runtime together\n\nUpdated {now}. **Audio quality and computational scalability are equal research priorities.** The new 48-point paired pilot completed in {cost["measured_full_cycle_wall_seconds"]/60:.1f} minutes within its 45-minute ceiling. {decision}\n\nReusing the decoder graph preserved every frozen raw WAV exactly and reduced matched generation-loop wall time by **{speed:.2f}%**, with peak allocated memory {mem_a:.2f} → {mem_b:.2f} GiB. The fixed spectrum repair changed WER {s["raw50"]["error_percent"]:.2f}% → {s["anchor25"]["error_percent"]:.2f}% and UTMOS {s["raw50"]["quality"]["utmos"]:.3f} → {s["anchor25"]["quality"]["utmos"]:.3f}. A speed gain is not a quality solution, and a quality gain must retain attack strength.\n\n'+table+f'\nThe generation search is still required for each new recording. Including measured feature extraction and repair, 1,000 similar new clips are forecast at {forecast["new1000_similar_recordings_hours"]:.2f} hours and ten audio hours of teacher data at {forecast["teacher10_audio_hours_allocation_hours"]:.2f} allocated GPU-hours, before additional corpus scoring or any student training. No reusable student was trained. See [complete joint results and cost breakdown](21_quality_efficiency_results.md); the interface now includes a **Runtime & scale** view and the new recordings.\n\nPublication is also an explicit research objective: these engineering/repair changes alone do not establish novelty. See [publication positioning](22_publication_positioning.md) for the next-method contribution and evidence plan.\n\nThe historical expanded-cycle account follows.\n'
 pos=text.index('\n## The original implementation');text=text[:pos]+intro+text[pos:];text=text.replace('The unresolved problem is **keeping the audio good enough at the same time**.','The unresolved problems are **keeping the audio good enough and making the computation scale in practice**.');text=text.replace('Register one quality-focused change','Register one quality/efficiency change').replace('The next study should test a specific content/quality hypothesis, with a fixed baseline, compute budget and 48-point pilot.','The next study should test a specific content/quality and efficiency hypothesis, with measured throughput forecasts, a fixed baseline, compute budget and 48-point pilot.');text=text.replace('No new GPU research run was launched for this reporting/interface request. The only long-lived process added is the audio web server.','The earlier reporting/interface request launched only the audio server. The new continuation ran the separately registered paired pilot above; its explicit status, logs and exit receipts are under `execution_tradeoff/`.');p.write_text(text)
 p=P/'HANDOFF.md';text='\n'.join(line for line in p.read_text().split('\n') if not line.startswith('**Active continuation, 26 October 2026:**'));update=f'\n**Continuation completed {now}.** Read [21_quality_efficiency_results.md](21_quality_efficiency_results.md) and `execution_tradeoff/results.json` first for the latest paired 48-point experiment. It completed normally under its 45-minute ceiling; {decision} Matched decoder graph reuse cut loop time {speed:.2f}% with exact frozen-output parity; spectrum repair changed WER/UTMOS as recorded in the new report. Runtime and quality remain equal priorities. The user also explicitly requires publication-level contribution/novelty in the speech/NLP theme; read [22_publication_positioning.md](22_publication_positioning.md) before selecting the next method. `JOB_STATUS.json` describes the older expanded queue and remains frozen; current cycle status/exit receipts are `execution_tradeoff/status.json` and `execution_tradeoff/exit_receipt.json`. Interface regeneration now uses `execution_tradeoff/refresh_interface.py` so the new study is classified, and delivery uses `execution_tradeoff/build_interface.py` for staging immutable assets before atomic index replacement. Do not rerun its preserved staging directory; choose a new staged build for a future revision. The server remains on port 8888.\n';pos=text.index('\n',text.index('# BeyondWaveform'));p.write_text(text[:pos]+update+text[pos:])
 p=P/'audio_browser/README_AUDIO_BROWSER.md';text=p.read_text().replace('67 scored conditions','70 scored conditions').replace('2,664 scored recordings','2,808 scored recordings').replace('44 use the 48-recording cohort','47 use the 48-recording cohort').replace('No new GPU research run was launched.','The earlier interface-only delivery launched no research run; the new continuation ran a separately registered paired pilot.');text+='\n## Latest quality/efficiency continuation\n\nThe new 48-point pilot and Runtime & scale tab extend the catalogue. Regenerate with `/opt/venv/bin/python /workspace/improvement/execution_tradeoff/refresh_interface.py`; this preserves the original builder and adds the new study and cost queries. Read `../21_quality_efficiency_results.md` for the completed experiment. The latest staged build and atomic index receipt is `../execution_tradeoff/interface_build_receipt.json`; its prior served metadata and all old audio/sidecars are preserved. Use a new staging path for a future rebuild. No new server or port is needed.\n';p.write_text(text)
 print(decision)
